## Live constraints

- `202` cannot precede commit. Publish failure must not change `202` or the receipt.
- `granot-lifecycle-events*` wake-ups are consumed by `api/queues/granot-lifecycle-consumer.ts`, which accepts only `{ receipt_id }` and calls the shared drainer. Five-minute cron `/api/cron/granot-lifecycle-drain` scans due work. Mongo claim/fence selects the single winner.
- Processing disabled means no claim; capture and due work remain intact.
- Processing and shadow default true. All eight effect flags stay false.
- Shadow, retry, and requeue must not create, update, cancel, or un-cancel a Booking.
- Capture, identity, and planner have no production Lead/Booking/Cancellation write path. Matched-Lead field writes exist only through `synchronizeLeadFromGranot` when live + Lead writes + all eight gates authorize them. Authorized create-if-missing writes exist only through `createLeadFromGranot` when live + Lead creation + all creation gates authorize them. Checked-in defaults keep shadow true and Lead writes/creation false. Unit 19 does not enable Registry `create_if_missing` or change indexes.
